s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-14T14:04:35Z","updated_at":"2025-10-14T14:04:35Z","body":"I would like to take this issue and will raise the PR soon.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3402057363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"vishalgoyal316","id":48381880,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzgxODgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48381880?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316","html_url":"https://github.com/vishalgoyal316","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3409890122","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/142835#issuecomment-3409890122","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/142835","id":3409890122,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87LPstK","user":{"login":"vishalgoyal316","id":48381880,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzgxODgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48381880?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316","html_url":"https://github.com/vishalgoyal316","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T09:00:39Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T09:02:17Z","body":"This script has some critical shape mismatches and wrong parameter values:\n\n1. **Batch Size Mismatch**\n   grad_output shape: (5, 4, 3) - batch_size=5\n   input shape:       (2, 5, 8) - batch_size=2\n   \n   Issue: The batch dimension must be identical across grad_output and input.\n\n2. **Weight First Dimension (in_channels)**\n   input shape:  (2, 5, 8) - in_channels=5\n   weight shape: (2, 5, 8) - first dimension=2\n   \n   Issue: For transposed convolution, weight shape must be \n   (in_channels, out_channels/groups, kernel_size). The first dimension\n   of weight (2) doesn't match the in_channels from input (5). This breaks\n   the mathematical requirement that weight filters must process all input\n   channels.\n\n3. **Weight Second Dimension (out_channels)**\n   grad_output shape: (5, 4, 3) - out_channels=4\n   weight shape:      (2, 5, 8) - second dimension=5\n   \n   Issue: The weight's second dimension should be out_channels/groups (4/1=4),\n   but it's 5. This violates the convolution constraint where the number of\n   output filters in the weight must match the number of output channels.\n\n\n4. **bias_sizes = [1] - Incorrect Size**\n   grad_output shape: (5, 4, 3) - out_channels=4\n   bias_sizes: [1]\n   \n   Issue: The bias must have one value per output channel. With out_channels=4,\n   bias_sizes should be [4], not [1]. \n   \n   Fix: bias_sizes = [4]\n\n5. **stride = [65534] - Unreasonably Large**\n   Value: 65534 (close to 2^16)\n   \n   Issue: This is astronomically large for a stride value. Stride controls how\n   many positions to move between convolution operations. Typical values are 1-3.\n   Such a large stride causes:\n   - Integer overflow in internal calculations\n   - Massive memory allocation attempts\n   - Extremely sparse output (skipping 65534 positions per step)\n   - Poor performance and numerical instability\n   \n   Fix: stride = [1] (no downsampling) or [2] (common for downsampling)\n\n6. **dilation = [536870912] - Causes Memory Issues**\n   Value: 536870912 (exactly 2^29, or 512 MB if each position is 1 byte)\n   \n   Issue: Dilation controls spacing between kernel elements. This extreme value:\n   - Creates massive memory requirements (gigabytes or terabytes)\n   - Causes integer overflow in address calculations\n\n7. **output_padding = [1879048192] - Violates Constraints**\n   Value: 1879048192 (approximately 2^30.8, or ~1.75 GB)\n   \n   Issue: output_padding adds extra size to one side of the output (only for\n   transposed convolution). It must satisfy: output_padding < max(stride, dilation)\n   \n   With stride=[1] and dilation=[1], we need output_padding < 1, so valid values\n   are only [0]. The original value of ~1.8 billion violates this constraint by\n   a factor of 1.8 billion.\n\n8. **groups = 0 - Primary Error (Non-positive)** ⭐\n   Value: 0\n   \n   Issue: groups must be strictly positive (> 0). The groups parameter controls\n   how input and output channels are partitioned:\n   - groups=1: standard convolution (all inputs connected to all outputs)\n   - groups>1: grouped convolution (reduced connections and parameters)\n   - groups=in_channels: depth wise convolution\n   \n   Mathematical constraint: groups must divide both in_channels and out_channels.\n   With groups=0, the division would be undefined (division by zero).\n\n**Correct Parameters:**\n\ngrad_output: (2, 4, 8) - batch=2, out_channels=4, output_length=8\ninput:       (2, 5, 8) - batch=2, in_channels=5,  input_length=8\nweight:      (5, 4, 3) - in_channels=5, out_channels/groups=4, kernel_size=3\n\nbias_sizes = [4]                      # ✓ Matches out_channels=4\nstride = [1]                          # ✓ Reasonable value (was 65534)\npadding = [1]                         # ✓ OK as-is\ndilation = [1]                        # ✓ Standard dilation (was 536870912)\ntransposed = True                     # ✓ OK as-is\noutput_padding = [0]                  # ✓ Valid: 0 < max(stride, dilation)\ngroups = 1                            # ✓ CRITICAL: Must be > 0 (was 0)\n\nTo handle Core dump issue, I will raise PR for better error message for groups < 1 values (and add test case for the same).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3409890122/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"vishalgoyal316","id":48381880,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzgxODgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48381880?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316","html_url":"https://github.com/vishalgoyal316","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"actor":{"login":"vishalgoyal316","id":48381880,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzgxODgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48381880?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316","html_url":"https://github.com/vishalgoyal316","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vishalgoyal316/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T19:17:22Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T19:17:22Z","source":{"type":"issue","issue":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/165669","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/165669/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch